WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.834
We're about
to play a game of "Catchphrase,"

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.701
but Tariq and I need partners.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.167
Tariq, we found
a great one for you.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.567
He is the voice of Superman
in the new movie,

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.767
"DC: League of Super-Pets,"

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.601
which is in theaters
this Friday.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:17.300
Give it up for John Krasinski!

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.400
-Oh!

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.501
Oh!
-How are you?

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:26.033
♪♪

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:29.267
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:31.868
-Don't vote on those.
They're voting.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:34.968
[ Laughs ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:38.834
My partner is a Grammy-nominated
singer/songwriter

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.634
whose new album, "Surrender,"
is out on Friday.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.200
Please welcome Maggie Rogers!

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:50.334
♪♪

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.567
-Tariq, Maggie.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.501
-So happy to see you.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.033
-John, Maggie.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.434
Guys, here's how the game works.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.033
I'm gonna start the round
by pressing start

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:01.200
on this buzzer right here.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.734
John, you'll draw a clue
from the top of the pile.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.400
You have to get your partner
to guess the clue

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.167
as quickly as possible,
then hand the buzzer

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.634
to the person on your right.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.100
If you're holding the buzzer
when it goes off,

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.400
your team loses that round.
We're gonna play three rounds.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.133
Let's take our positions.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:15.334
I'm here.
-All right.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.467
-Where are you?
You'll be across from me, right?

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.834
When you're ready,
I'm gonna press start,

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:19.868
and you're gonna draw the first
clue and go for this.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:21.033
All right?
-Let's do it.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.334
-All right, here we go.
-Okay.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.501
-Come on, bud, we got this.
-All right, I'm ready.

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.100
-Let's connect.
-I'm ready.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.167
I'm ready.
-Yes. Tap in. Yes.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.133
-Go.
-Oh, okay.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.400
-Um...
A fish that's very angry.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.501
Has angry teeth.
-Shark.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:34.734
-But they're little
and a lot of them.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.033
-Oh, piranha.
-That's right.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.734
-Wow! Very calm.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.434
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.033
-He's an ogre with green ears.
-Shrek.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.267
-Yep.
-Wow.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.067
-Oh, that's cheating.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:45.868
-It's what pickles are
before they're pickled.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:46.868
-Cucumbers.

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.934
-Damn
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.601
-When you're really angry
in a car at other people.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:52.767
-Road rage.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:55.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.567
-What's up?
-It's not -- It's --

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:57.934
you don't have this
on your yard,

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.434
you have it in your...
-In your house.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.868
On your porch.
-It's when I'm selling things.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:05.067
[ Cymbals crash ]
-Oh, a yard sale.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.200
A sale.
Yard sale.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.868
-In -- But in the --
-Garage sale.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.667
-That's it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.734
-It's a game, and you have to --

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.267
you're talking and you're giving
instructions, and it's a guy.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.501
-Charades.
-Who's telling you instru--

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:20.133
[ Buzzer ]
-Simon Says.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.734
[ Sad tuba ]
-No, no.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.801
No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.400
-Can't believe you didn't
get "garage sale"

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.801
from "selling stuff
out of your garage."

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.801
-But I still got it, though.
I like how you said,

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.801
"Simon Says"
and still lost the round.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:31.968
-That was a good hint.
That was a good hint.

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:35.000
Yeah, I was,
"Hm, sounds like 'garage sale.'"

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.367
[ Laughter ]
"Uh, 'Garage sale?'"

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:38.067
"Yes!
How'd you guess that?"

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.667
-That was a purposeful stall.
-Yes, yes.

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:40.968
-That was a great, great,
great hint.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.400
-It's like at the end
of Hot Potato where you're like,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.834
"Got him."
-It's part of our technique.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.200
-You know what happened, though?

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.968
You started off so calm.
-Thank you.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.968
-And then we all --
no, we all were calm.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.067
And then we were really good.
And then -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.033
-And then I ruined it?
-No, yeah, kind of.

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:54.601
-Are we gonna edit
that part out?

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.567
-No, we're gonna leave that in.
-We're still calm.

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.634
-That was real.
It shows that you're human.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.267
-Cool as a pickle
before it's pickled.

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:01.767
-That's what I'm talking about.
-Come on, let's do it.

00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:03.601
-That was a clue earlier.
[ Beeping ]

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:05.734
-Uh...

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:09.167
Okay, these are, you know,
chocolate, graham cracker,

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.601
marshmallow thingies.
-Oh, boy. S'mores?

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:16.467
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:17.868
-I'm in a pool.
-Oh, boy.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.000
-Oh, I see.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.133
-We've all heard this story.
-Great.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:24.067
-Playing a game
where I yell and you respond.

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.734
-Oh, um.
Uh...

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.234
Uh...
-Yeah.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:31.667
-Ralph Lauren makes a line of
clothing that sounds like this.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:32.801
-Marco Polo.
-That's correct.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:36.200
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.000
-This is a type of cookie.
-Graham cracker.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.234
-But it's also
based on candy bar.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:44.400
-Uh, uh, Rocky Road --
What is that thing?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.934
-Yes.
It satisfies you.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.501
The candy bar satisfies you.

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.033
-Oh, dang, a Snickers --
Snickerdoodle!

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.901
-Yes! Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.734
-It's a dance that you do.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.434
-Macarena!

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.033
-Okay. Um, um, um...
It's a TV show --

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:57.734
[ Buzzer ]
-Oh!

00:03:57.734 --> 00:04:00.667
[ Sad tuba ]
[ Laughs ]

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.601
-We still got it.
We still got it.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.000
-I have a question.
-What?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.000
-Is it cheating
if she did the macarena?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.200
-No!
-I didn't say anything.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.767
-She didn't say anything.
-She was...

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.000
-No.
-We'll let her live.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.968
-That was good.
But I did --

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:14.400
I will say, Tariq,
that was a good hint.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.400
It's a TV show.
-Get out of here!

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.000
[ Laughter ]
-Should've got that one.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.367
You should've got that one.
All right.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.100
-Okay.
-Let's do one more.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:23.767
-We're doing great.
Don't listen to this.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.300
-All right.
Come on, Jimmy, let's go.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.601
-It is a, you know,
a plate that, you know --

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.801
another word for a spaceship.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.400
-Rocket.
-No, a plate.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.667
Like a plate.
-Oh, a UFO.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:33.834
-No, like a plate.
Like, what do they call it?

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.067
[ Laughter ]
Like, what do they call it?

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:38.434
An aerial plate.
Aerial plate.

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:41.000
-Am I -- Am I an idiot?
-It's a plate-shaped thing

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.334
that aliens are on.
God!

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.167
-UFO, UFO.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.534
-No, John!

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:48.968
Old school!
What do they call it?

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:50.133
Old school.
Back in the day.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:52.434
-Still a UFO.
-No, you see a UFO,

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.601
he lands in a what?

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:57.968
"Dude, I saw an aerial plate."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.167
-I got nothing.
-How you doing?

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:00.501
Everything good.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:03.334
-It's dinnerware in the sky.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.334
Dinnerware in the sky!

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:06.968
-Flying saucer.
-Flying saucer!

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.367
-God, yes!
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.934
Geez Louise!

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:12.901
-The winners -- me and
Maggie Rogers, right there!

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:14.901
Come on.
[ Ding! ]

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.100
-I am so sorry.
-Dude, you're good.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.367
You were good, bud.
-I am so sorry.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:18.901
-My thanks to John Krasinski --

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.100
You're about
to have a heart attack.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.100
Maggie Rogers, Tariq Trotter!

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.601
We're talking to John
after the break.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.133
Stick around, everybody!

